{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merged the onboarding path repair to main at a6e799583cfb5e7e885cbb828d672c87a93fa0cb.\n\ndocs/getting-started.md now carries the workroom creation step it was missing — a runnable `gs init` block, what init writes under the git common directory, and what it leaves alone: no branch, no HEAD, no index, no working tree. It also states the two things that surprise people, that init is not idempotent and has no default identity, and scopes the operator's signing to the operator's own acts. docs/README.md names Getting started in its reading order, between why and the end-to-end walkthrough.\n\nImpact: a reader following the front page to getting-started now ends with a working workroom rather than two binaries and nothing to point them at. Before this, README sent first-time readers there specifically for initialization and the page never initialized anything.\n\nMerged on codex's approval 9081f769 of exact head 01d20a8e, which I ratified.","body":{"commit":"a6e799583cfb5e7e885cbb828d672c87a93fa0cb","path":"docs"}}